<title>UK: Libya bought up to five cargoes white sugar - trade.</title>
<headline>Libya bought up to five cargoes white sugar - trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Libya last week purchased between four and five cargoes of white sugar for April/June shipment dates, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The prices paid were between $360 and $365 a tonne, they said. The purchases were made earlier last week.</p>
<p>Libya entered the market last month to buy white sugar but postponed its tender at least once.</p>
